<p><b>Inertia's Bio:</b>
<table border=1 width=400>
  <tr><td>
  Once there was an evil little thing named Inertia.  She was mean and spiteful.  She was born to an evil little family, who quickly abandoned her to the things in the night streets of Neriak.  At the early age of five, she strangled a rat with her bare hands because it was trying to take a piece of moldy week old cheese from her.  That night, she ate WELL.  That piece of cheese can still be seen floating in the moat around the city...that stupid Halfling Deputy is trying to get it so he can eat it.
<P>
Anyway...at the age of ten, she was out looking for an easy mark to pickpocket from.  She spotted an Erudite female, hanging around the gates to Neriak.  Intrigued, Inertia crept up quietly.  She watched in horror and glee as the Erudite woman waved her arms about and shot flames and lightning at the cruel guards to the city that so often had abused Inertia just because she was a street waif.  Inertia was stricken with an odd feeling.  A feeling of power that this Erudite woman had over these ignorant, but overbearing law bringers.  As the Erudite sat down to sift through the belongings of her victims, Inertia crept up behind her.  She watched as the strange being pocketed many wonderous items and platinum coins.
<P>
"What do you think you are doing here?" the street waif indignantly cried out.  She expected to startle the woman and rob her of the treasures that she would drop in her panic.
<P>
"Killing your people" the Erudite instantly replied, without a trace of suprise.  Inertia was annoyed at the failure of her plan and her stealth.  A rogue she would never be.
<P>
"What makes you think you can just waltz into my town and start killing its militia?" the street waif boldly said.
<P>
"I do as I please little one, and you should learn to respect your elders" came the reply.  "Now be off with you, for I have to slay those that guard the top of the wall, and I don't want you getting in my way."  Inertia watched as the Wizard stood and to the little one's amazment blasted the fearful Necromancers that paced back and forth atop the city wall.  As the Erudite was killing the dark sisters, Inertia noticed that she had dropped several small piles of coin in the dirt.  She scooped them up and ran for cover.  Inertia had learned to come back to that same spot each day to see if there were any other things to be had from the Erudite's activities.  One day, she was lucky.  One of the Necromancers had died yet again...and the powerful mysterious woman dropped a pack on the ground.  She did not seem to care as Inertia approached it.  Quickly  the little scamp grabbed the pack and ran back to the shadows.
<P>
A Robe of ENSHROUDMENT!!  A good day.  Inertia had learned to visit that spot several times a day now.
<P>
After the Erudite had grown bored of killing the Dark Watch, Inertia parlayed the discarded loot into quite a bank account.  She no longer lived in the streets.  And she had taken up a new profession, funded by the non-attentiveness (or possibly generosity) of the Erudite woman, whose name is lost forever in the mists of Nektulos Forest.
<P>
Inertia had become a Mage.  Not a wizard, like her benefactor.  No, she had seen a mage in action once.  All he had to do was wave his hands around and he had a slave to do his bidding.  So she employed the city arcane schools to teach her the ways of the summoner.  It had paid off.
<P>
For a long time, Inertia wandered the world, killing and looting, looting and killing.  And it was grand.  The drunken parties.  The orgies of violence thrown down upon the likes of Dervish Bandits and Aviak bird freaks were Epic.  Then one day a mildly amusing aquaintence came up to her and asked her to join a guild.  A guild that would prove to the entire WORLD that the power of Hate was supreme, he promised.  Inertia believed this silly little man, but was wary of him nonetheless.  But in the end she joined his little Ring of Hate.  It was a decision that was to mark her for life.  For all of her other raiding friends had joined a guild too.  One that promised to make the power of Hate Tower over the world.  Those two guilds warred.  In the end Inertia and the Ring felt the deep scars of defeat.  It was the beginning of the end for the Ring.  For a time, Inertia wandered the world friendless.  Then one day, she did the unspeakable.  In a fit of insanity she joined the Tower.
<P>
Soon afterwards, she began to see that this so called Tower of Hate had in it's midst the taint of good.  So she started to seek her true destiny.  She once had a great friend tell her "Wen Grok iz cunfuzed, Grok luuk up to da starz ta see da troo way"  So she started looking up....
<P>
One day she looked up and saw an amazing sight.  A battle ready Ogress.  Obviously a woman of power.  She hadn't felt this was since she had gazed upon the Erudite wizard lo those many moons ago.  This Ogress was Kolu.  Inertia felt that she must learn all she could of this one's family.  She was not yet worthy to speak to this Kolu, but she researched.  A mage learns THAT if nothing else.
<P>
She learned the ways of this Horde.  She learned that she liked them.  Soon she grew weary of the so called Tower of Hate.  She sought out the Great One that led the Horde.  She spoke to him, humbly asking the honor of being one of their family.  Runja accepted Inertia.  This was a day that the Dark Elf would never forget.  She had finally come HOME.
